A||N||5||Bob Englert||auto trans side cover||||1||
Z||000000||Bob Englert||10-23-2001||02:11 PM||||My 87 GT appears to be leaking severely around the auto transmission side cover.  It appears that a previous owner had this off and it was resealed with RTV, which has failed.<P>A local transmission shop told me the cradle had to be dropped to remove and replace this side cover.  Can this cover be removed from the top without disturbing the cradle?  I think this is the cover that is removed when the TCC solenoid is replaced.  <P>Thanks for any advice.  I need to get this fixed before my car is declared a bio hazard!<P><BR>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl<p>[This message has been edited by Bob Englert (edited 10-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||10-23-2001||02:20 PM||||Oh, just pour about a gallon of Epoxy or Fiberglass resin over the cover.  That should seal it up nicely!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>||||reg||12
Z||000002||Bazooka||10-23-2001||03:24 PM||||Bob,   Jack the front of the car up on the passengers side and remove the wheel well liner/push pins to have access to the mounting bolts of the side pan. Its best just to replace the gasket.<BR>*********************************<BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Bob Englert:<BR><B>My 87 GT appears to be leaking severely around the auto transmission side cover.  It appears that a previous owner had this off and it was resealed with RTV, which has failed.<P>A local transmission shop told me the cradle had to be dropped to remove and replace this side cover.  Can this cover be removed from the top without disturbing the cradle?  I think this is the cover that is removed when the TCC solenoid is replaced.  <P>Thanks for any advice.  I need to get this fixed before me car is declared a bio hazard!<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-23-2001||07:44 PM||||There's no reason at all to remove it from the car. Someone's just being an ass. People change the TCC solinoid in the car all the time. In fact you may as well replace that and the switch while the cover is off. (Unless you think that's why it was off last time in what case you just need to fix the cover.)<P>For RTV to work right, the surface has to be clean. most people don't clean well enough and the RTV invariably starts leaking again.<P>You can do it all from the top but it's bloody awkward. working thru the wheel well makes it much quicker. Long socket extensions and a universal joint help to. That will get the wrench out where you can turn it easier.<P>Before you put the parts back together, clean the metal with alcohol or brake parts cleaner. Just put some on a rag then wipe things down good to get all the oil off the sealing surfaces.<P>Best fix is a new gasket and some Permatex High Tack gasket adhesive to hold it in place long enough to get things lined up.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bob Englert||10-23-2001||11:00 PM||||Thanks to all.  This looks like a much easier fix than I thought it would be.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||10-24-2001||12:50 AM||||Bob, let me know if you need some help.  I'll even bring the epoxy!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
